--- A program's own names spelled as a part's declarations were once
--- inlined are the program's own (spec, Importing): `lib/greet.co`'s
--- `loud` had been `lib_greet_loud` inside the program, so the program's
--- own `fn lib_greet_loud` was refused in the part's file ("'loud' is
--- declared twice") and its `lib_greet_count` was the part's `count`
--- given again; and `lib/shop/cart.co` beside `lib/shop_cart.co` had
--- been one prefix, their `total`s one name. A part's declaration is its
--- path and its name joined by a mark no name holds (`lib·greet·loud`),
--- in both modes.
use lib/greet
use lib/shop/cart
use lib/shop_cart

struct lib_greet_Greeting [words, times]

fn lib_greet_loud[n]
    return n * 10

lib_greet_count = 7

log[greet.loud['a']]
log[lib_greet_loud[5]]
log[greet.count + lib_greet_count]
log[greet.make['hi'].words]
log[lib_greet_Greeting['ho', 3].times]
log[cart.total[[1, 2, 3]]]
log[shop_cart.total[[1, 2, 3]]]
